form10-k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79.bin","sha256":"88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79"}},{"id":"bfb97463b3f6a3e2f2d4ca0796ba44f209408bba61dd31b35075d13d61e31f9c","quote":"Cost of sales consists primarily of manufacturing cost, product purchase costs, and depreciation of surgical instruments. Cost of sales also includes reserves for estimated excess inventory and inventory on consignment that may be missing and not returned. Cost of sales increased by 1%, or $0.6 million, to $49.7 million for the year ended December 31, 2025 from $49.1 million for the year ended December 31, 2024. The increase was due primarily to increased charges for excess and obsolete inventory, partially offset by reduced product costs resulting from the transition to internal production in 2025 compared to 2024.","context":"Cost of Sales","section":"The following table sets forth our results of operations for 2025 and 2024 (dollars in thousands):","block":589,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-013792","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-31","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001453593","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1453593/000149315226013792/form10-k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79.bin","sha256":"88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79"}},{"id":"86ac33abbdfb2e9dfa45b008594520c8743dbb9b0b4c45c530e178680b8dc55e","quote":"Gross profit as a percentage of revenue increased to 62.9% for the year ended December 31, 2025 compared to 58.2% for the year ended December 31, 2024. Of this increase, 530 basis points were due to sales mix and greater scale, partially offset by a decrease of 260 basis points due to increased charges for excess and obsolete inventory.","context":"Gross Profit","section":"The following table sets forth our results of operations for 2025 and 2024 (dollars in thousands):","block":591,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-013792","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-31","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001453593","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1453593/000149315226013792/form10-k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79.bin","sha256":"88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79"}},{"id":"351361be21dce9113ada31b420977f26f246dca27013a64ec126a88a8613db44","quote":"General and administrative expenses consist primarily of personnel costs for corporate employees, cash-based and stock-based compensation related costs, amortization, and corporate expenses for legal, accounting and other professional fees, as well as occupancy costs. General and administrative expenses increased 2%, or $0.7 million, to $29.4 million for the year ended December 31, 2025 compared to $28.7 million for the year ended December 31, 2024. This increase is primarily attributable to $2.2 million of additional expense related to various compensation plans, $0.7 million of additional bad debt expense, $0.7 million of additional legal fees associated primarily with the divestiture transactions with Companion Spine, partially offset by $1.2 million of reduced stock-based compensation expense.","context":"General and Administrative","section":"The following table sets forth our results of operations for 2025 and 2024 (dollars in thousands):","block":593,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-013792","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-31","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001453593","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1453593/000149315226013792/form10-k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79.bin","sha256":"88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79"}},{"id":"fbd178c035b826b015e392f5cc640ca94546c0feeb004d1154b5574e763badc8","quote":"Sales and marketing expenses consist primarily of sales commissions; personnel costs for sales and marketing employees; costs for trade shows, sales conventions and meetings; travel expenses; advertising; and other sales and marketing related costs. Sales and marketing expenses decreased 8%, or $3.7 million, to $45.5 million for the year ended December 31, 2025 compared to $49.2 million for the year ended December 31, 2024. This decrease is primarily due to reduced commission expense of $3.9 million resulting from revenue mix and $2.1 million of reduced compensation expense related to headcount, partially offset by $2.9 million of additional consulting fees.","context":"Sales and Marketing","section":"The following table sets forth our results of operations for 2025 and 2024 (dollars in thousands):","block":595,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-013792","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-31","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001453593","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1453593/000149315226013792/form10-k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79.bin","sha256":"88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79"}},{"id":"5cfff2bd513211a378955705fbda57f3c2f84545b25055e283192758ebbd4e4d","quote":"Research and development expenses consist primarily of internal costs for the development of new product technologies. Research and development expenses decreased 12%, or $0.3 million, to $2.1 million for year ended December 31, 2025 compared to $2.4 million for the year ended December 31, 2024.","context":"Research and Development","section":"The following table sets forth our results of operations for 2025 and 2024 (dollars in thousands):","block":598,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-013792","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-31","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001453593","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1453593/000149315226013792/form10-k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79.bin","sha256":"88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79"}},{"id":"93c4120f2c0add326d14ca20642d592697701b0ab4178b5f1cd939b281ce02f1","quote":"Interest expense for the year ended December 31, 2025 decreased $0.5 million to $3.7 million as compared to $4.2 million for the year ended December 31, 2024. This decrease resulted primarily from reduced borrowings on our revolving line of credit, as well as prepayments totaling $8.0 million on our term loan, during 2025 as compared to 2024.","context":"Interest Expense","section":"The following table sets forth our results of operations for 2025 and 2024 (dollars in thousands):","block":600,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001493152-26-013792","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-31","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001453593","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1453593/000149315226013792/form10-k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79.bin","sha256":"88e2bcf4707aa60223e696db5ff9c54e46ca2088cfb1532d5329c08846d16a79"}},{"id":"d67aea95b5ec6662c1b2a45652d02f78b1088050dc353334b2fb311e17298f13","quote":"We recognized $0.1 million of interest income during the year ended December 31, 2025 related to the Companion Spine Note receivable from the sale of assets related to our Coflex and CoFix products to Companion Spine.","context":"Interest Income","section":"The following table sets forth our results of operations for 2025 and 2024 (